@smenzer 
As per http://prebid.org/dev-docs/modules/gdprEnforcement.html
If I define rules for storage (Purpose 1) and personalized ads (Purpose 4) then it would mean following

1) Enforce that the user consents to DeviceAccess as an activity and consider their per-vendor selection. Here if user doesn't give consent to Appnexus than we do not allow Appnexus bidder to do usersync, access localstorage and cookies.
```
pbjs.setConfig({
  consentManagement: {
    gdpr: {
      ...
      rules: [{
        purpose: "storage",
        enforcePurpose: true,
        enforceVendor: true
      }
    }
  }
});
```
If I put your counter proposal in api, below rule would mean that if user doesn't give consent to Purpose 4 then we allow user id's to be shared with all bidders.
```
pbjs.setConfig({
  consentManagement: {
    gdpr: {
      ...
      rules: [{
        purpose: "personalizedAds",
        enforcePurpose: true,
        enforceVendor: true
      }
    }
  }
});
```
Am I correct in understanding this ? If yes then this is little bit confusing to me as out of 4 purposes there is one purpose which behaves opposite when using rules api.
